@cc [owner:id13,label:security] trusted-source-bindings
Every notification MUST match an enrolled notification configuration and exactly one trusted bucket/prefix binding before any content access or DFS mutation. Tenant credentials and read grants MUST come only from that binding, never from object metadata. Prefix bindings within a bucket MUST NOT overlap.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;concurrency] source-version-publication
GCS generations and metagenerations MUST remain exact decimal strings. Generations MUST NOT be compared numerically across object versions. Before reading the DFS cursor and live GCS metadata, an importer MUST acquire shared ownership for the tenant/bucket/object and revoke and drain any prior registered DFS session. Every mutating session MUST be registered while ownership is current. Publication MUST use one Rename of a completely staged file whose metadata contains the observed cursor; directory grant inheritance MUST switch reader visibility with that rename. Deletion MUST use one Remove; confirmed namespace absence is its durable state. Cursor conflicts MUST acquire a new fenced session and reread both systems. Acknowledgements MUST follow confirmed publication or an equal current observation. Historical notifications MUST NOT remove a live replacement. No unfenced writer may mutate importer-owned directories.

@cc [owner:id13,label:error-handling] worker-transport-errors
The standalone relay and worker configuration, notification processing and transport boundaries MAY throw validation or remote-operation failures. The message-handler boundary MUST catch these failures, classify them without logging source content or credentials, and leave failed messages unacknowledged for retry/dead-letter delivery. Startup failures MUST terminate the process. This exception does not apply to other front code.

@cc [owner:id13,label:performance;concurrency] bounded-worker-admission
Pull batches, concurrent handlers, object bytes, manifests and chunk requests MUST have explicit bounds. Acknowledgement leases MUST be renewed while a handler runs. Shutdown MUST stop admission and drain admitted handlers or leave their messages unacknowledged.

@cc [owner:id13,label:architecture;performance] event-driven-replication-only
Automated replication MUST remain notification-driven. Health checks MUST NOT list source objects, scan DFS inventory, publish repair events or write directly to the DFS importer. Repairs and backfills require a separate operator action.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security] canary-source-write-boundary
The legacy direct-delivery health runner MUST restrict source writes to the reserved `.dust-gcs-dfs-canary` object under each explicitly selected trusted binding prefix. Canary replacement MUST use the previously observed generation as a write precondition, or zero for initial creation. The replication worker MUST NOT acquire source-write permissions to run canaries.

@cc [owner:id13,label:backend;error-handling] canary-completion-and-health-failures
A legacy direct-delivery canary MUST succeed only after observing its newly written generation and metageneration as live in the durable DFS cursor before its deadline. Existing or deleted cursor state MUST NOT count as success. Failed, missing, stale or invalid health observations MUST report an unhealthy result. Health transport adapters MAY throw validation or remote-operation failures; the health-check boundary MUST catch them without logging credentials or source payloads. This exception is limited to health transport and configuration boundaries.


@cc [owner:id13,label:security;concurrency] workspace-object-routing
Relay ordering keys MUST use the trusted workspace binding and exact object name with the versioned workspace/object encoding. Generations MUST NOT participate in keys. Relay configuration MUST NOT accept importer credentials. Ordered workers MUST recompute and validate keys before source reads or DFS operations.

@cc [owner:id13,label:concurrency;error-handling] ordered-delivery-boundaries
Same-key handlers MUST execute sequentially within a process while different keys share bounded slots. Relay acknowledgements MUST follow confirmed downstream publication. Ambiguous or failed publication MUST leave the source message unacknowledged. Ordering MUST NOT replace distributed ownership, DFS session fencing or live reconciliation.

@cc [owner:id13,label:logging;performance] bounded-replication-metrics
Metric tags MUST NOT include workspace, object, bucket, generation, notification or message identifiers. Process liveness MUST track processing progress independently of backend success, and shutdown MUST immediately withdraw readiness before draining.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security;backend] front-canary-boundary
The production canary MUST create its own unique file in the explicitly configured private-upload workspace through normal FileResource methods. Updates and cleanup MUST operate only on that run's resource. It MUST NOT mutate pre-existing files, list source objects, scan DFS inventory, or call the DFS importer. The canary MUST attempt cleanup after success or failure. SIGKILL and ambiguous writes MAY leave artifacts requiring operator cleanup; no automatic repair scan is permitted.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security;testing] front-canary-evidence
Successful create and update checks MUST compare unique nonce bytes using a live DFS reader session and prove denial to a separate valid reader session of the same tenant. Authentication failures MUST NOT count as permission denial. Delete success MUST require DFS namespace absence and live-source absence. Cloud drift checks MUST cover both delivery hops and retained DLQs. Missing, stale, malformed or inaccessible observations MUST fail closed. Canary configuration, transport and producer adapters MAY throw; the run boundary MUST catch failures without logging credentials or payloads, emit a failed outcome and attempt cleanup.

@cc [owner:id13,label:api;security] dfs-grpc-projection
DFS operations MUST use front/lib/dfs and the canonical typed protobuf protocol at dfs/protocol/proto/dfs.proto. They MUST NOT use a separate HTTP facade, PoC bincode protocol, or invented wire operations. Import publication MUST preserve source-version-publication; a client-side Validate followed by Apply MUST NOT be represented as an atomic compare-and-swap. Each Apply MUST contain only one operation, and ambiguous mutations MUST NOT be blindly replayed. Reader credentials MUST be separate session keys, not tenant-management keys. Canary reads MUST compare bytes and attributes returned in the same Read snapshot.


@cc [owner:id13,label:concurrency;security] durable-import-ownership
Redis ownership MUST use server time, unique owner tokens, atomic owner checks and logical lease deadlines without expiring session records. Takeover MUST retain the previous session ID until RevokeSession confirms all admitted mutations have drained. A new session MUST NOT mutate before atomic registration. Expired ownership MUST NOT be renewed or registered. A stale holder MUST NOT clear or release its successor's record. Session records MAY be deleted only after confirmed revocation. Redis errors MUST fail closed. Deployment MUST preserve acknowledged ownership history without eviction or rollback and route session calls to one authoritative DFS session domain; lost history requires stopping and fencing all import writers before recovery.

@cc [owner:id13,label:security] inherited-import-grants
Each binding MUST use distinct preprovisioned final and staging directories and an importer-only writer subject. Both directories MUST have exactly DENY rw and ALLOW writer rw; only the final directory additionally allows each trusted reader r. Import attempts MUST verify these explicit grants before source reads. Staged files MUST have no explicit grants, inherit private staging access during writes, and inherit final-directory access only through the publication rename. The worker MUST NOT change grants as part of an import.
